==History==
2018
*The Electro Dragon was once available in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Electro Dragon Draft Challenge]], which started on 27/10/2018. In this [[Tournament|challenge]], gameplay was similar to a regular Draft Challenge, except that one of the players was able to choose who would use the Electro Dragon. If the player achieved at least 6 wins, they obtained the Electro Dragon early.
*The Electro Dragon [[Cards|card]] was generally released on 9/11/2018.
*On 3/12/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (3/12/2018)|Balance Update]], decreased the Electro Dragon’s hitpoints by 5% and increased its first attack time interval to 0.7 seconds (from 0.2 seconds).
2019
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]], added a card render to the Electro Dragon's card info screen.
2021
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
2022
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Electro Dragon from Electro Valley to Spooky Town.
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
2024
*On 7/10/2024, the [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (7/10/2024)|October 2024 Update]], added the Electro Dragon’s Evolution.
2025
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], decreased the Electro Dragon's hitpoints by 0.1%.

