==Trivia==
*The Electro Dragon resemble [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_dragon dragons from European cultures]. being reptilian legendary creatures, often depicted as winged, horned, and capable of breathing fire. However, the Electro Dragon breathes lightning bolts instead.
*The word "Electro" come from the Greek word "''ἤλεκτρον''" (elektron), meaning amber, referring to its electrostatic capabilities. Electricity was first detected through electric fish from as far back as 2750 BCE where Ancient Egyptian texts described them as the "protectors" of all other fish. At around 600 BCE, Thales of Miletus made a series of observations on static electricity, from which he believed that friction rendered amber magnetic, in contrast to minerals such as magnetite, which needed no rubbing. Thales was incorrect in believing the attraction was due to a magnetic effect, but later science would prove a link between magnetism and electricity. Electricity would remain little more than an intellectual curiosity for millennia until 1600, when the English scientist William Gilbert wrote ''De Magnete'', in which he made a careful study of electricity and magnetism, distinguishing the lodestone effect from static electricity produced by rubbing amber.
**The Electro Dragon is 1 of 11 [[cards]] associated with electricity, with the others being [[Electro Spirit]], [[Zap]], [[Tesla]], [[Zappies]], [[Electro Giant]], [[Lightning]], [[Electro Wizard]], [[Sparky]], [[Wizard Trio]], and the [[Goblinstein]].
***In the Spanish, Italian, Russian, Arabic, Portuguese, and Thai language settings of the game, the Electro Dragon's name translates to "Electric Dragon". In the Chinese and Finnish language settings of the game, the Electro Dragon's name translates to "Thunder Dragon" and "Lightning Dragon" respectively.
*It is 1 of 3 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that are “miniature” versions of another troop in Clash of Clans, the others being the [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]] and [[Baby Dragon]]. They are smaller versions of [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Electro_Dragon Electro Dragon], [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/P.E.K.K.A P.E.K.K.A], and [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Dragon Dragon], respectively.
**The Electro Dragon is a reference to the eponymous troop in Clash of Clans. However, the Electro Dragon in Clash Royale is a less durable infant, only hits up to three targets with its chain lightning, has the same damage for all three hits, stuns on strike and doesn't inflict death damage.
*The Electro Dragon is one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the [[Archers]], [[Knight]], [[Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Flying Machine]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], Zappies, [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], [[Balloon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Electro Dragon has been featured in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]] outside of the card. More specifically:
**The Electro Dragon is 1 of 4 troops that has been featured in the [[Treasure Hunt#Dragon Hunt|Dragon Hunt]] sub-[[:Category:Modes|mode]] of the Treasure Hunt game mode, the others being [[Skeleton Dragons]], Baby Dragon, and [[Inferno Dragon]].
**The Electro Dragon is 1 of 14 troops that has been featured with a [[Buff#Rage|Rage]] [[buff]], the others being Electro Spirit, Giant, Zappies, [[Guards]], Giant Skeleton, Goblin Giant, Wall Breakers, Electro Giant, Mega Knight, Ram Rider, Electro Wizard, Sparky, and Royal Ghost.
*Acoording to the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4M_PPPCN19E Electro Dragon's intro video], and its description, it is implied that the Baby Dragon, Electro Dragon, and Inferno Dragon are brothers, with the Electro Dragon being the middle child.
*According to the Electro Dragon's intro video, the Electro Dragon is the Electro Wizard's pet dragon.
*After each attack, the spikes on the Electro Dragon's backlight up in sequence, similar to a Sparky's charge. This is merely a visual indicator; its attack does not charge like Sparky's attack does.
*The Electro Dragon is 1 of 4 troops that can deal damage to multiple units with one attack without an area damage radius, the others being Electro Spirit, Hunter, and Electro Wizard.
*The Electro Dragon is the subject of 2 [[Emotes]].
**From the Electro Dragon's Emotes, the Electro Dragon produces its lightning by sneezing, unlike its counterparts who produce fire by burping.
*The Electro Dragon was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|deck]] of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/C5qBcdcErfM?si=e37mhAgNKAA5kMJI Clash Royale League 2018 Tournament], by a player called Lciop.
*The Electro Dragon is currently the only Dragon unit in Clash Royale to shoot a projectile other than fire.
*In an update on 24/11/2025, the attack sound belonging to both the Electro Dragon and [[Electro Spirit]] was mysteriously removed (As was [[Graveyard|Graveyard's]] deploy sound). While Graveyard's sound has been restored, the other two strangely have not had their sound restored yet.

